.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_CAPTURE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_capture_into ,
.Nm dtfl_event_link_new ,
.Nm dtfl_event_link_new_sync ,
.Nm dtfl_event_link_pusher ,
.Nm dtfl_event_link_free
.Nd capture a timely stream for later replay
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_stream_capture_into "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_event_pusher p" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_event_link *
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const dtfl_type *type"
.Ft dtfl_event_link *
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new_sync "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const dtfl_type *type"
.Ft dtfl_event_pusher
.Fn dtfl_event_link_pusher "dtfl_event_link *l"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_event_link_free "dtfl_event_link *l"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_capture_into
records every event of
.Fa st
through the event pusher
.Fa p :
each received message becomes a
.Em Messages
event, and each change to the stream's frontier a
.Em Progress
event.
A later
.Xr dtfl_event_link_replay 3
reconstructs the stream and its frontier in another scope, so a captured
stream can be moved between dataflows, serialized, or examined after the
computation has finished.
.Pp
A
.Vt dtfl_event_pusher
is a pair of callbacks and a context.
.Fn dtfl_event_link_pusher
returns a pusher that appends to an event link, the in-memory log created
by
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new .
Events hold times of class
.Fa tc
and records of
.Fa type .
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new_sync
creates a link whose pushes and reads are serialized with a mutex, so a
stream captured on one thread can be replayed or extracted on another.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_event_link_free
drops a link and every event it holds.
A long chain is freed iteratively, not by recursion.
The context in
.Fa ctx
is released by its destructor when the capture operator is dropped.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_event_link *link = dtfl_event_link_new(tc, dtfl_type_u64());

/* in one dataflow: capture a stream */
dtfl_stream_capture_into(stream, dtfl_event_link_pusher(link), DTFL_NOCTX);

/* in another dataflow: replay it */
dtfl_stream *replayed = dtfl_event_link_replay(link, scope);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
An invalid stream or a type mismatch is a programming error and calls
the panic hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_event_link_extract 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_event_link_replay 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn capture_into
operator and the
.Vt EventLink
and
.Vt EventPusher
types of
.Pa capture/event.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A stream and its capture operator belong to the worker thread that built
them.
A plain event link, like a worker handle, belongs to one thread.
A link made with
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new_sync
is thread-safe: it may be pushed on one thread and replayed or extracted
on another.
